  "description": "Find the nth super ugly number given a list of primes. A super ugly number is a positive integer whose all prime factors are in the given list of primes.",
  "target": 12,
  "pseudocode": "1. let ugly = [1]\n2. let pointers = new Array(primes.length).fill(0)\n3. while (ugly.length < n) {\n4.   let next = min(primes[i] * ugly[pointers[i]])\n5.   ugly.push(next)\n6.   for (i) if (next == primes[i] * ugly[pointers[i]]) pointers[i]++\n7. }",
